@format 1
@id section-modification.set-end-on-selected-section
@title Set End on selected section
@section Section modification
@area In Split tab
@entry end-dispatch
@summary Modify the end boundary of the currently selected Split section; Set End branches that create a new section are excluded.
@related section-modification.common.compass-buttons, section-modification.common.keyboard-shortcuts, section-modification.common.apply-modified-state, section-creation.set-end-creates-section
@tag section
@tag split
@tag modification
@tag end

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment
@alias piece = Cadroue.Core.LPiece

[end-dispatch] setEnd dispatch request <input>
~ This starts with setEnd dispatch request.
[Technical explanation]
= The request came from the Split Compass End button or the currently bound SectionEnd shortcut.
> dispatch-guard

[dispatch-guard] Active Split flow guard <decision>
~ The program checks active Split flow guard.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowShortcutDispatch requires a command-active flow with a loaded spool and active section UI before invoking PFlowEndSet @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / setEnd
? "Rejected" > dispatch-rejected
? "Accepted" > handler-guard

[dispatch-rejected] Set End ignored <output>
~ This path ends with set End ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= No section operation is called.

[handler-guard] Modification preconditions <decision>
~ The program checks modification preconditions.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowEndSet requires section editing enabled, a loaded spool, and a nonblank source path before calling LSegmentEndSet with cursor, color, and overlap policy @ flow.PFlowEndSet(...)
@ flow.PFlowColorRead(...)
@ property flow.PFlowOverlapAllowed
? "Editing disabled or media/source unavailable" > handler-rejected
? "Preconditions accepted" > selection-check

[handler-rejected] Set End blocked <output>
~ This path ends with set End blocked.
[Technical explanation]
= Existing section state is unchanged.

[selection-check] Existing section selected <decision>
~ The program checks existing section selected.
[Technical explanation]
- LPieceEndSet creates a new ending section when the active index is null; only a non-null active index enters the existing-section modification branch @ segment.LSegmentEndSet(...)
@ piece.LPieceEndSet(...)
? "No selected section" > creation-outside
? "Section selected" > start-bound-check

[creation-outside] Creation branch excluded <output>
~ This path ends with creation branch excluded.
[Technical explanation]
= This path belongs to Section creation, not Section modification.

[start-bound-check] Cursor must stay after selected start <decision>
~ The program checks cursor must stay after selected start.
[Technical explanation]
- The existing-section branch rejects a cursor at or before the selected section start @ piece.LPieceEndSet(...) / selected start check
? "Cursor at or before start" > invalid-end
? "Cursor after start" > next-start-limit

[invalid-end] No end modification <output>
~ This path ends with no end modification.
[Technical explanation]
= The selected section is unchanged and no modification log is written.

[next-start-limit] Respect later-section limit <decision>
~ The program checks respect later-section limit.
[Technical explanation]
- LPieceLimitRead starts with the requested cursor as ceiling; when overlap is disabled it finds any other section start after the selected section's old end but before the cursor. The request is rejected if the cursor would extend beyond that returned limit @ piece.LPieceLimitRead(...)
@ piece.LPieceEndSet(...) / limit check
? "Cursor passes a later section start" > limit-rejected
? "Cursor allowed" > replace-end

[limit-rejected] End extension blocked <output>
~ This path ends with end extension blocked.
[Technical explanation]
= The selected section is unchanged and no modification log is written.

[replace-end] Replace selected end boundary <process>
~ This step handles replace selected end boundary.
[Technical explanation]
- Copy the section list and replace the selected LPiece with the same data except LPieceEnd=cursor; shrinking, extending, or reapplying the same end all use this accepted plan @ piece.LPieceEndSet(...) / existing-section plan
> map:section-modification.common.apply-modified-state
